<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH BREWER RADEGAST 1996 NET RISES.</title>
<headline>CZECH BREWER RADEGAST 1996 NET RISES.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary results for year</p>
<p>ending December 31, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit	     162.56	    vs	  95.78</p>
<p> Gross profit	   272.22	    vs	 196.00</p>
<p> Operating profit	  n/a	    vs	 219.68</p>
<p> Production	   1,577.98	    vs     1,353.74</p>
<p> Total assets	 4,050.61	    vs     2,646.23</p>
<p> Basic capital	  794.32	    vs	 794.32</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Pivovar Radegast a.s. Radegast</p>
<p>is one of the largest Czech beer brewers, partially owned by</p>
<p>Britain's Bass plc . The results were calculated under</p>
<p>Czech accounting standards. Radegast shares are listed on the</p>
<p>main market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
